<title>NORWAY: DnB profits up with strong Norway economy.</title>
<headline>DnB profits up with strong Norway economy.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's biggest commercial bank, Den norske Bank ASA (DnB), reported a 5.3 percent rise in nine-month net profits on Thursday to 2.20 billion crowns ($345 million) from the same year-ago period.</p>
<p>Return on equity was 22.1 percent, with earnings per share at 3.44 crowns.</p>
<p>Third-quarter profits were 689 million crowns, a rise of 264 million relative to the first nine months of 1995.</p>
</text>
